{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-bond-order-le-three","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:bond-order-le-three","kind":"proposition","title":"Bond order bounded by spatial dimension","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-embeddable-knot-operator"],"tags":["bond-order","spatial-dimension","orthogonal-channels","p-block","sigma-pi"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Molecular.orthogonal_channels_le_dim","text":"bond-order-le-three.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:bond-order-le-three\"></a><p><em>Each bond channel embeds as a direction in the ambient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code>-space, with distinct channels mutually orthogonal. Orthogonal nonzero vectors are linearly independent, so their number cannot exceed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim_{\\mathbb{R}} \\mathbb{R}^3 = 3</code>. At most three mutually-orthogonal channels embed — one axial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code> and two transverse <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code>. The bond order is bounded by the spatial dimension. No <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-block bond exceeds order three.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/bond-order-le-three.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"18.5.7","page":"b/prop-bond-order-le-three","qa":{"counts":{"pass":92,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Observations.EmbeddableKnotOperator.orthogonal_channels_le_dim","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/EmbeddableKnotOperator.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
